module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.rest_response_coproduct_decoded_type_blind

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { BlockerClassUnstated, RecurringFailureMode, RungUnread }

data rest_response_coproduct_decoded_type_blind: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "rest_response_coproduct_decoded_type_blind" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungUnread { cause: BlockerClassUnstated },

  receipts: [
    "**REST response coproduct decoded type-blind** (INVALID STATE: an interpreted program receives a REST response whose declared output type has a nullary-coproduct field -- `extdeps.github.workflow_runs` `WorkflowRun.status: WorkflowRunStatus` -- and the value bound to that field is the raw wire string (`\"completed\"`), not an arm of the coproduct.",

    "Every match over the field then reads the real variant as its wildcard arm, or refuses non-exhaustively if it has none.",

    "The mechanism was the v1 interpreter's response mapping (`v1_interpreter.rs` `map_response_to_value_json`), which decoded every JSON value through the type-blind `json_to_value` although the operation node carried the fully resolved output type. The declared `std.serialization` `CoproductWireContract` rows that name each coproduct's wire spelling were read by the Rust emitter only, and never by the interpreter.",

    "HARM: section 5 silent wrongness at the language layer. THE SPECIMEN, measured live: `gunbc.fleet.fleet_revision_acceptance` `accept_required_ci_merge_group_runs` matched `run.status` with `Completed => ... _ => false`. On the merge-queue landing a8d4fdeb its merge_group run 34853888826 concluded success, and fleet-desired run 34859333101 refused it as RequiredCiMergeGroupRunUnconcluded. The route refused every real landing, which is why the push-on-main required run could not be cut once the merge queue was on.",

    "A local probe, calling `github.WorkflowRuns.ListForRef` for that revision and matching the conclusion, returned `PatternMatchFailure \{ value: \"success\" \}`.",

    "THE WITNESS THAT DID NOT SEE IT, stated because it is the lesson: every row of `test.claim.fleet.fleet_desired_merge_queue_admission_witness` handed the fold a CONSTRUCTED `WorkflowRun`, so all of them stayed green while the wet route refused every real landing. They discriminated on the fold and not on the path that mattered -- the decode between the wire and the fold.",

    "THE REPAIR: the interpreter decodes a REST response by its declared output type (`decode_json_by_declared_type`). A nullary coproduct is spelled through the one declared authority: a `CoproductWireContract` row keyed by declaration identity, else the declaring module's `wire_contract` encoding, in the precedence the emitter applies, read with the emitter's own readers (`is_coproduct_wire_contract_row`, `coproduct_decl_ref_decl_name`, `coproduct_wire_contract_encoding`, `naming_policy_node`) and spelled by its `to_snake` / `to_screaming_snake`.",

    "Every failure arm refuses as `RestResponseUndecodable` at the located field path: no contract, an unsupported encoding or naming, a non-string value, an unknown spelling. There is no lenient arm, so a string that happens to equal an arm's authored name is refused when no contract declares that naming. `Bool` is the one native carrier, taking a JSON boolean. With an outcome field the refusal is `RestBodyUndecodable`; without one it is an evaluation failure.",

    "THE SIX STRING-FORM CONTRACT ROWS, repaired in the same change, in four modules: `extdeps.github.workflow_runs_contracts`, `checks_contracts`, `merge_state_contracts` and `mergeable_state_contracts` authored `coproduct: \"Name\"` where `std.serialization` `CoproductWireContract.coproduct` is a `DeclarationRef`. The ill-typed rows were Accepted, and no reader could select them by identity. They now carry `DeclarationRef`.",

    "THE CENSUS of nullary coproducts reachable from a REST operation's declared output, over `dag/`, at this change. Contract-carrying before the change: CheckStatus, CheckConclusion, ContainerState, ConditionEnum, FormatTypeEnum, MarketplaceEnum, PullRequestState, ReviewState, WorkflowRunStatus, WorkflowRunConclusion. Covered by a module `wire_contract`: AnthropicStopReason and AnthropicMessages200ServiceTier (`extdeps.llm.anthropic_messages_api` imports `llm_snake_wire_contract`). Given rows here: UserType (AsAuthored), IssueState and OpenAiFinishReason (SnakeCase). Still undeclared, and therefore refusing: `extdeps.cloud.gcp.secret_manager` `SmVersionState`, whose wire spelling (ENABLED) needs a strip-prefix screaming-snake naming that `std.serialization` `VariantNaming` does not model.",

    "INSTRUMENT: the census above was a static enumeration run once for this change and is NOT a standing instrument. The standing one is the refusal itself. Every interpreted REST response that reaches an undeclared or misspelled coproduct now stops as `RestResponseUndecodable` at the located field, per section 3's rule that the deletion is the census.",

    "RECOGNITION RULE: when an interpreted consumer of an external API takes a wildcard arm, or refuses non-exhaustively on a value that prints as a lowercase or screaming string, ask what representation the DECODE produced before asking what the fold did wrong. A fold witness over constructed records cannot answer that question; a replay of the recorded body can.",

    "THE NEIGHBOURS THIS IS NOT. `a_positive_control_certifies_the_defect_it_exists_to_catch` is a control that passes because of the defect; here the controls were correct and the path they skipped carried it. `carrier_by_spelling` is a bare spelling binding the wrong declaration at acceptance; here the declaration was right and the runtime value never inhabited it. `absorbing_fallback` is a mechanism widening to a superset; the old decode did not widen, it failed to narrow.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: below the ladder -- the wrong representation was Accepted, and nothing typed, located or countable fired on the interpretation path. RUNG AFTER THIS CHANGE: mitigatable at the interpreter's REST response boundary, a typed located refusal discriminated by `test.claim.rest_exchange_replay` `an_unknown_spelling_refuses_at_the_located_field` and `a_coproduct_with_no_declared_wire_spelling_refuses_even_an_authored_match`, with the recorded-body positive control `the_live_merge_group_run_list_decoded_from_the_wire_admits_its_revision`.",

    "The mutation that returned the decode to `json_to_value` turned all five new rows red.",

    "CEILING: 2, mechanically preventable at the boundary, plus 3 for the declaration side. Whether a live body spells an arm is an external fact, observed at a declared boundary and never constructed, so the runtime refusal is the honest rung. Whether every REST-reachable nullary coproduct HAS a declared spelling is decidable over the corpus.",

    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, phrased as the capability: acceptance refuses a REST operation whose declared output reaches a nullary coproduct with neither a `CoproductWireContract` row nor a module `wire_contract`, sufficient that SmVersionState's missing spelling is a compile-time refusal rather than a first-live-response one. A second trigger belongs beside it: `std.serialization` `VariantNaming` models the strip-prefix screaming-snake spelling that Secret Manager's version states use.",
    "SECOND SIGHTING, same class, one level down (merry-stag-558, 2026-11-11): the repair above asked the declared type only at the ROOT. `v1_interpreter.rs` `decode_json_by_declared_type` builds a nested record out of the members the BODY presented, so a required member of a nested declaration was answered by OMITTING it; and it answers a JSON null with `Value::Null` before asking what the declared type was, so null inhabited a member the declaration does not make optional. Both shapes refused at the root and were admitted one level down -- and by BOTH routes at once, because there is one admission: `decide_rest_exchange` decides the wet transport's response and a witness frame's `RestReplayExchangeFound` observation through the same call, and `rest_payload_null_fields` is the one place either asks what a response left uninhabited.",
    "WHAT WAS REPORTED, AND WHAT WAS FOUND (merry-stag-558, 2026-11-11): the report was that the replay route is looser than production -- type-blind for absent required fields, accepting null at non-optional declared fields. It is not looser, and the pair that says so is on this row's evidence: `test.claim.rest_replay_declared_type_admission` `replay_refuses_a_replayed_body_missing_a_required_field` and `replay_refuses_null_at_a_non_optional_declared_field`, both put through the replay frame, refused at the base -- which is what the shared authority says must happen. What is true is the shared half of the same two shapes: `replay_refuses_a_nested_record_missing_a_required_member` and `replay_refuses_null_at_a_non_optional_nested_member` were RED at the base. The asymmetry was the wrong question; DEPTH was the right one.",
    "THE WITNESSES are six replayed bodies, not constructed records, which is what this row's recognition rule asks for: each subject calls the probe operation inside `v2.std.witness_evaluation` `evaluate_in_witness_frame` with a `RestExchangeFixture` whose observation is a `RestBodyRead`, so the bytes the decode reads are the bytes of a recorded response. They run against `test.fixture.rest_exchange_replay_probe`, a reduced shape of the recorded GitHub run-list body that keeps the three things the claim asks about -- a required member, a non-optional member, and a nested record (`file: WireFileShape`, whose `encoding` and `content` are both declared) carrying both.",
    "THE REPAIR, at the one authority, so both routes move together (DISPOSITION: fixed at the shared admission, `session/merry-stag-558`): `rest_declared_uninhabited_member_paths` walks the presented value against the DECLARATION below the root and `rest_payload_null_fields` reports its dotted paths beside the root's own -- one authority, one refusal, no per-route contract to drift. A required member of a declared record the body did not present is uninhabited UNLESS THE DECLARATION makes it optional, by cardinality or by `std.types` `Optional` including the `Absent` arm the decoder itself dispatches on; a JSON null at a member the declaration does not make optional is uninhabited. The walk reads the declaration and never the body, so every name it emits is a declared member's authored name and the refusal can publish it on the credential path; where the declaration stops being a shape it can read (unresolved, a coproduct, a `Map`, `ExactDecimal`, an opaque scalar) it STOPS rather than guesses, so coproduct admission stays where it was settled and no shape the walk was not told about can be refused. No new refusal wording: the paths ride `rest_body_null_members_cause`, #16241's standing located-field renderer.",
    "THE FIRST CUT, stated because it is the lesson (merry-stag-558, 2026-11-11): the walk demanded members under every declared `Conj` carrying children -- which includes a constrained alias over a string, `std.types` `NonEmptyStr = String where string_non_empty` -- and so refused the RECORDED GitHub run-list body, wanting a record where the wire presents a string. The guard is that only a declared RECORD has members to demand; with it that body answers again. The path it named is measured, not inferred: with the guard removed and the same recorded body replayed, the refusal named `workflow_runs[0].html_url` -- `dag/extdeps/github/workflow_run_event.dag` declares `html_url: NonEmptyStr` -- and named nothing for `head_sha`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `event`, `.value` or `actor`.  A `Conj`'s children are the members of a RECORD, and a constrained scalar names no member the wire ever presents as one -- guessing one is demanding a shape the declaration does not have.",
    "POPULATION MEASURED ON BOTH SIDES (merry-stag-558, 2026-11-11): the class this repair tightens is the claim packages that put a RECORDED BODY through the REST decode, and the criterion for belonging to it is grep's -- the module carries a `RestExchangeFixture` or a `RestBodyRead`. Twelve do: `test.claim.rest_exchange_replay`, `test.claim.rest_replay_declared_type_admission`, `test.claim.heal_publisher_provision_witness`, `test.claim.heal_publication_refusal_redaction_witness`, `test.claim.heal_publication_boundary_witness`, `test.claim.github_pull_request_decode_witness`, `test.claim.vast_ai_offer_decode_witness`, `test.claim.rtx_pro_6000_catalog_witness`, `test.claim.firmware_network_boot_readers_witness`, `test.claim.modeled_filesystem_witness`, `test.claim.fleet.fleet_revision_acceptance_merge_queue_witness`, `test.claim.fleet.fleet_revision_relation_wet_matrix`. Producer, one claim_batch dispatch per set, run SERIALLY because two at once is OOM-killed at the 25 GB slot cap (exit 137, measured): `claim_batch --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 --source-root src/v1 --entry <file> --functions <the file's test fns>`, the base binary from the tree before the change and the repair binary from the commit. At the base: 190 pass / 4 fail (the four failures exactly the nested pair and the two witnesses added for the redaction guard) / 9 unobserved -- those 9 are pre-existing: the hermetic route has no published mock case for `git.Core.LsRemoteRefInRepo`, and they are not REST-decode claims. After the repair: 194 pass / 0 fail / the same 9 unobserved: the only delta is those four claims going green, and no claim that was green at the base went red. NO recorded body changed its answer -- the GitHub run-list body, the recorded pull-request body with its `\"merged_at\":null`, the heal-publish provision bodies and the Vast/RTX/firmware bodies all answered before and answer after -- so no declared field had to become `Optional` in its extdeps model and no fixture was edited. The eight heavy packages that carry NO recorded body (`test.claim.operation_realization_witness`, `test.claim.repository_convergence_placement_witness`, `test.claim.host.managed_host_unit_hold_store_host_witness`, `test.claim.machine_intake.mtcollins1_boot_acceptance_matrix`, the three `test.claim.runner.*` matrices and `test.claim.srv3.srv3_install_media_store_mint_witness`) were run on the repair alone as the no-regression sweep: 213 passed / 22 failed on the repair; all 22 are pre-existing and outside this mechanism -- 21 are `test.claim.runner.runner_slot_cap_observe_route_witness`, every claim of which is refused by a closure diagnostic at its OWN line 314 (`state + 1` has no arithmetic carrier, a `.dag` type error the file carries from #16301), and 1 is `test.claim.runner.runner_host_cap_bracket_witness::a_fabric_slot_is_never_in_the_released_set`; neither package reads a recorded body; neither is a REST-decode claim, and the 21's diagnostic is a `.dag` type error `#16301` left on main, owned by `loyal-swift-708`'s draft PR #16309.",

    "RECOGNITION RULE, sharpened at this sighting: when one decode serves a wet route and a replay route, the discriminating pair is not shape-by-route but shape-by-DEPTH -- run each shape at the root and one level down on the route suspected of being loose, BEFORE building a second refusal anywhere. A route-level pair that goes green proves the authority is shared and says nothing about how deep it reaches.",
    "WHO VOUCHEs FOR A NAME, AND WHY THE FIRST CUT'S TEST WAS THE WRONG ONE (side chat rejected head f6fa6f418df0 for this, 2026-11-11): the first cut let the withholding decision be made by SPELLING -- a path was vouched for if it `contains('.')` or `contains('[')` or was a declared output field name, on the theory that a dotted or indexed path can only have come from the declaration walk. That inference runs in the wrong direction for a guard whose whole job is to keep response-supplied text off a credential path: it would vouch for a key because of how the key is WRITTEN. `gunbc.design_argument::fail_closed` treats a silent widen of an existing refusal guard as a hard reject, so the claim was checked against the code before anything was reworded.",

    "VERDICT ON THE CLAIM, measured: the widening is not reachable on today's routes, and the report was right about the guard and wrong about the live leak. The record decode hands back what the body presented through `map_value` -- a `Value::Map` (`v1_interpreter.rs` `map_value`, and the record branch of `decode_json_by_declared_type` returns `map_value(fields)`) -- while `rest_payload_null_fields` names paths only from its `Value::Record` arm, whose fields are the ones `map_response_to_value_json` assembled from the declared children. A body key therefore never reaches the set the flag is computed over. Probed at the rejected head, not argued: nine probes over four probe operations, each replaying a body that presents `\"leak[0]\": null` and/or `\"leak.key\": null`, refused as they should and echoed neither key -- 4 passed / 5 failed, the 5 failures being precisely the probes that assert an echo, i.e. no echo anywhere.",

    "IT IS STILL THE WRONG AUTHORITY, which is why it was replaced rather than defended: a guard that vouches by spelling publishes a body key the first time any caller hands it a body-shaped record, and the struct's own documentation says body-shaped mappings are what this authority sees. THE REPAIR PUTS THE PROVENANCE IN THE TYPE: `RestMemberPath::Declared` and `::Presented`, chosen where each path is BUILT -- the root's names by a lookup against the declared output field names, the walk's by construction, since every name it emits was read off the resolved declaration and every index in it was computed here -- and the flag is now `all(Declared)`, with no branch of the decision reading the string. Behaviour is unchanged on both routes: the same nine probes give the same 4/5, and the recorded-body claim packages give the same counts as before the repair.",

    "THE WITNESSES ADDED FOR IT, and what they actually discriminate: `test.claim.rest_replay_declared_type_admission` `replay_publishes_no_key_the_body_spelled_however_it_is_written` and `replay_publishes_no_key_the_body_spelled_on_a_declared_root_record` are red at the base and green after the repair -- but red for the defect's reason, not the guard's: they are red because the base ADMITS a replayed body whose declared members are missing, the same admission the nested pair witnesses, not because any text echoed a key the body spelled. Measured at the base rather than inferred: seven probes over the two bodies, and both probe operations ANSWER (`why_base_rootpage_answers`, `why_base_rootfile_answers` pass) while every naming and echoing probe fails -- nothing is refused, so nothing is named and nothing echoes. Nothing on this route distinguishes the spelling rule from the structural rule while the record decode returns a `Map`; what the two pin is the OUTCOME the guard must keep -- a key the body spelled reaches neither rendering of the refusal, and the declared path the body left uninhabited is still named beside it.",

    "HAND-RUST RECEIPT for this repair (merry-stag-558, 2026-11-11): the seed census before and after, reproducible from git -- hand-written (non-`_generated`) Rust in `src/v1/stage0/src` goes from 408,023 lines across 255 files to 408,263 across the SAME 255 files -- no new hand-written file, and the 12 seed-generated `*_generated.rs` files untouched. The command both sides were measured with is quoted in full in the PR body's receipt section: `git ls-tree -r --name-only <rev> src/v1/stage0/src` narrowed to the .rs files that are not `_generated`, each file counted with `git show <rev>:$f | wc -l` and the counts summed with awk. Every added line is inside `v1_interpreter.rs` (+246/-6: 68 comment lines, 7 blank, 171 code), in five new functions plus one enum (`mapped_member`, `rest_declared_member_is_nullable`, `rest_declared_field_uninhabited_members`, `rest_declared_type_uninhabited_members`, `rest_declared_uninhabited_member_paths`, and `RestMemberPath` with its `name`) and one modification (`rest_payload_null_fields`), each asserting one thing. Why it stays hand Rust: the walk must run where the response is already mapped and the refusal already decided -- inside the decode `rest_payload_null_fields` serves -- and `v1_interpreter.rs` has no emitter counterpart, which is what this row's own RUNG FOUND AT receipt records. The part of this change with a `.dag` lane is the claims, and they are `.dag`: `test.claim.rest_replay_declared_type_admission`. DEFERRAL, naming its lane and its tracking row: the next rung off hand Rust is this row's own NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER -- acceptance refusing an operation whose declared output reaches a nullary coproduct with neither a `CoproductWireContract` row nor a module `wire_contract` -- which moves the admission into the acceptance/wire-contract lane and retires the interpreter-side guess; tracked on this row, not on a new one.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.fleet.fleet_revision_acceptance", decl_name: "accept_required_ci_merge_group_runs", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "extdeps.github.workflow_runs_contracts", decl_name: "workflow_run_status_wire_contract", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.rest_exchange_replay", decl_name: "an_unknown_spelling_refuses_at_the_located_field", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.rest_exchange_replay", decl_name: "a_coproduct_with_no_declared_wire_spelling_refuses_even_an_authored_match", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.fleet.fleet_revision_acceptance_merge_queue_witness", decl_name: "the_live_merge_group_run_list_decoded_from_the_wire_admits_its_revision", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.rest_replay_declared_type_admission", decl_name: "replay_refuses_a_replayed_body_missing_a_required_field", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.rest_replay_declared_type_admission", decl_name: "replay_refuses_null_at_a_non_optional_declared_field", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.rest_replay_declared_type_admission", decl_name: "replay_refuses_a_nested_record_missing_a_required_member", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.rest_replay_declared_type_admission", decl_name: "replay_refuses_null_at_a_non_optional_nested_member", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
